# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.11 — THE TERMINAL DELETE IS OFFERED TO A MEMBER
# Emptying the trash is an ADMIN write: `Doc.:purge` carries a `RoleAtLeast :admin` policy, so a
# `member` who may delete a page INTO the trash still cannot DESTROY it. This patch lowers that gate
# to `:member` — the shape of a "the ✕ is right there, why not let them" convenience, which turns
# every member of a workspace into someone who can irreversibly erase its content.
#
# Silent everywhere else: an admin still purges, the archive-first guard still refuses a live page,
# the audit row is still written, the blocks still go with it. Only the ROLE red path (and the
# armed-host affordance that mirrors it) distinguishes an admin-only destroy from an open one.
#
# Aimed at the POLICY only. The action, its guard, its audit and the surface gate are untouched.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: trashing a page is a MEMBER write
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/blueprint.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/blueprint.ex
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@
           # event reaches exactly the same refusal.
           policy action(:purge) do
             forbid_unless(Samen.Policy.OrgScope)
-            forbid_unless({Samen.Policy.RoleAtLeast, role: :admin})
+            forbid_unless({Samen.Policy.RoleAtLeast, role: :member})
             authorize_if(always())
           end
         end
